Description: Ubuntu laptop protection with a native GNOME interface
 OctoShield provides a native GTK desktop application and a Bash command-line
 interface for configuring established Ubuntu security mechanisms. It helps
 manage named protection profiles, verified live status, scoped firewall rules,
 per-profile USB authorization, desktop locking, security updates, application
 confinement, and security-event notifications. Official release checks offer
 matching Debian packages for normal package-manager upgrades.
 .
 Each privileged change requires an explicit action and authentication. Package
 installation starts only the status observer and does not select a protection
 profile, enable security controls or enroll USB devices. The
 desktop application runs as the logged-in user and delegates narrowly scoped
 operations to a fixed PolicyKit-authorized helper.
 .
 Maintained by Vast Development Method as part of the Octoleo suite.
